INSERT INTO `quest_request_items` (`ID`, `EmoteOnComplete`, `EmoteOnIncomplete`, `CompletionText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(86585, 1, 1, 'That banner looks like it\'s been in a war!', 0),
(86758, 1, 1, 'How goes the huntin\'?', 0),
(86776, 1, 1, 'Gotta keep the forges going!', 0),
(87288, 1, 1, 'It is good to see you again! Are you here to trade?', 0),
(87760, 1, 1, 'We will finally have resolution to this mystery, and the animals will have peace at last!', 0),
(91740, 1, 1, 'Yes?', 0),
(91741, 1, 1, 'What\'s that you got there? It looks like one of my books.', 0),
(91743, 1, 1, 'Have you rescued my books yet, Braiknok?!', 0),
(91746, 1, 1, 'Yes?', 0),
(91752, 1, 1, 'Have you retrieved those stolen books yet?', 0),
(91920, 1, 1, 'Oh. You\'re back?', 0),
(91921, 1, 1, 'You return! I was beginning to come to terms with devolving into a ghoul.', 0),
(92706, 1, 1, 'What can I do for ya, $R?', 0),
(92744, 1, 1, 'I hope the murlocs did not give you too much trouble?', 0),
(92909, 1, 1, 'It\'s a mess out there, Theto! Did you collect the parts I need?', 0),
(95212, 1, 1, 'You look chilly, $C. How goes the hunt?', 0),
(95213, 1, 1, 'What\'s that you\'ve got?', 0),
(95214, 1, 1, 'I hope you\'ve got good news for me?', 0),
(95328, 1, 1, 'Do you have something for me, $C?', 0),
(95494, 1, 1, 'How goes the hunt?', 0),
(95495, 1, 1, 'Greetings, $C. What brings you up to my property today?', 0),
(95621, 1, 1, 'The remnants of Daelin Proudmoore\'s fleet who still fly his banner are just as rotten and barbaric as the admiral himself was before he died.$B$BI don\'t know why they are so far from Tiragarde, but it can\'t be good.', 0),
(95774, 1, 1, 'I have only memories now, but I will build a tribute to Olgra so that they never fade.', 0),
(96391, 1, 1, 'Oh what\'s this, then?', 0),
(96876, 1, 1, 'Something need doing?', 0),
(96877, 1, 1, 'Yes?', 0),
(96898, 1, 1, 'I\'d advise you not come into too much physical contact with those crystals. Even shattered and spent, the lingering magic in these necrotic crystals is highly dangerous.', 0),
(97003, 1, 1, 'It took the strength of six skilled fighters to defeat one of these creatures, and it still managed to fell four of us before we could put it down.$B$BIf these monstrous beasts were to appear in greater numbers, the damage that the qullboar could inflict upon the land could be catastrophic.', 0),
(97005, 1, 1, 'It took six of us to defeat one of these creatures, and it still managed to kill all but myself and one other before we were able to bring it down.$B$BThis far from alliance lands I should leave it well enough alone. Light knows I\'ll lose little sleep over a few tauren savages or orcish brutes. However, the honor of my fallen brothers demands action.', 0),
(97223, 1, 1, 'The Bloodtalon are known for their cunning and swiftness, and make fine companions when raised from egg to adult.$B$BUnfortunately adult raptors are very difficult to train, and I have tried to capture the Matriarch on more than one occasion. But she had become too dangerous of late.$B$BStill I hope to preserve her legacy by raising her children as companions here in Sen\'Jin.', 0),
(97249, 1, 1, 'I think we can win this one...', 0),
(97275, 1, 1, 'Alright, what\'s next... Black Lotus, Mountain Silversage...', 0),
(97282, 1, 1, 'It might come as a surprise that with a name like thunder lizard they shoot lightning instead of roaring like thunder.$B$BWell, they do. Shoot lightning, I mean.$B$BTrust me, it\'s a lesson you only get to learn once if you\'re lucky.', 0),
(97558, 1, 1, 'Have you gathered the skin I inquired about? Our stocks are running low.$B$BIt may seem odd to ask for murloc skin but it works well for internal membranes, or surfaces like cheeks or mouths.$B$BSimilarly, the duskbat wing membranes are especially suited for more delicate areas, like faces or fingers. It prevents the skin from being too... thick.', 0),
(97914, 1, 1, 'I can smell the sea on you, friend!$B$B<Baros laughs.>$B$BWhat brings you to Stormwind?', 0),
(97926, 1, 1, 'You have returned. What news comes from Stormwind?', 0),
(98025, 1, 1, 'Greetings $C - what may the Sentinels assist you with today? Perhaps you are here to inquire about the bounty on Jai\'vhanel?', 0),
(98028, 1, 1, 'I can sense something far older than you in my presence, $R... what have you brought me?', 0),
(98042, 1, 1, 'You look troubled. I am listening.', 0),
(98046, 1, 1, 'How may I aid you?', 0),
(98065, 1, 1, 'Please state your business. I have a city to run, and a people to lead.', 0),
(98298, 1, 1, 'Fangs, claws, gizzards. It makes no difference to me. The easiest way to study something is to see the guts yourself.', 0),
(98326, 1, 1, 'It\'ll be a hot day in Dun Morogh before I tell Paxton I lost his entire stockpile to a wendigo.', 0),
(98392, 1, 1, 'Have you wrested the amulets from the harpies\' leaders?', 0),
(98403, 1, 1, '<Tallonkai lowers his voice.>$B$BDoes Xethorr still walk freely?', 0),
(98407, 1, 1, 'A full assessment of the gnolls cannot be complete without facing the worst of their kind. Put those thrashers down!', 0),
(98459, 1, 1, 'Put yer backs into it! We set sail on my word!$B$BOh? What\'s that you have there, traveler?', 0),
(98461, 1, 1, 'What\'s all this about?', 0),
(98545, 1, 1, 'What\'s that? You say that Leonid sent you? Oh boy, haven\'t seen that crusty old soldier since Naxxramas was raining hell down on our heads.', 0),
(99050, 1, 1, 'Do you have the ingredients? I fear Eralya may not have long.', 0),
(99073, 1, 1, '<Eralya has stopped responding verbally. Only a weak, gurgled exhale confirms life.>', 0),
(99141, 1, 1, 'You\'d best have those reports in hand, or get out of my face.', 0),
(99152, 1, 1, 'You\'d best not be returning empty-handed. I either need the bones I asked for, or your body on a stretcher to confirm you at least gave it your all trying to get them.', 0),
(99156, 1, 1, 'Have you dealt with our little problem?', 0),
(99158, 1, 1, 'Why did the Light guide you here today?', 0);
INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(86574, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(86576, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(86585, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You found Ylva\'s body? Ah, the poor woman. She said she was going to show the troggs that Ironforge would never fall to their kind. She went looking for a few mountaineers who never returned from a patrol through trogg country. She was always too independent-minded to be cautious. Now we know what happened.$B$BI\'ll take the banner back and make sure it\'s cleaned up and displayed. You should take her weapon. May it serve you well against the troggs.', 0),
(86757, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(86758, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hah! You did it! I never thought that ol\' croc would get its comeuppance, but that does the trick!$B$BOh ah... y\'know, I had to get me another knife, but maybe that one will bring you some good luck. Why don\'t you hang onto it?', 0),
(86776, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, this is a relief! I should be able to keep the forge going now. Hopefully one of these days we\'ll get a trader bringing coal into town regularly!', 0),
(87288, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, these are wonderful. It is a shame to resort to violence with such majestic animals, but it is important to keep the roads safe, and these pelts will make beautiful blankets and shawls.$B$BHere, let me give you something to remember them. It is both soft and sturdy.', 0),
(87318, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(87491, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(87760, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This has been a long journey, Orangequake, but it was worth it.$B$BAt long last, you have wrested away the rod that the naga use to compel the sea creatures into their service. I will make sure it is destroyed, and the threshers and sea turtles can finally live in peace.$B$BThank you again. Your persistence has finally been rewarded, and I, personally, am grateful to you.', 0),
(88758, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(91723, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done, my friend. Let me try my calibrations again...', 0),
(91724, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It seems like everything is working properly. Thank you, Chonk.', 0),
(91740, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'We lost two members of the watch last week to the murlocs, $C. Hopefully with their leader slain, we can start pushing them out of Elwynn.', 0),
(91741, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hey! How did you end up with that? It\'s supposed to be on the shelf! Oh dear, the kobolds have been stealing my books again. They must want to eat them!$B$BThanks for bringing back the book, but what will I do about the rest of my missing collection?', 0),
(91743, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you so much! Here! Take one of these how-to books. I don\'t need them.$B$BBut there\'s still so many books missing. The kobolds don\'t seem to be eating them. So, why do they want them?', 0),
(91745, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Kobolds with books? Yah, I\'ve seen kobolds running back and forth with books, yelling at each other. They must be stealing them from the library inside the abbey.', 0),
(91746, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So, you took down Elmpaw? Very impressive, Ingmmar!$B$BLet me give you something in return for your trophy - I know a few collectors who will pay quite well to have this on their mantle once I\'ve prepared it.', 0),
(91752, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for returning these stolen books, Jødekong. I\'ll get them back to Brother Paxton at once.$B$BYou\'re becoming quite the hero around here. Great job!', 0),
(91758, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I can help ye\' track down this varmint. Let me whip somethin\' up for ye\'.', 0),
(91920, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The potion didn\'t work? Of course it didn\'t work. You brought me insufficient hearts. The recipe clearly calls for six. You brought three.$B$BHowever, I confess I hadn\'t considered applications for murloc parts until now...$B$B<Renferrel takes the eyes.>$B$BI can afford to sacrifice a few of my own hearts to get your Deathstalker\'s strength back.', 0),
(91921, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Quinn takes the potion and drinks it.>$B$BYes, I can feel it working.  I will soon be able to travel.$B$BYou have done me a great favor, Saixgone.', 0),
(92124, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yah, I overheard. I warned Brother Paxton three times about the kobolds tunneling under the abbey.$B$BIt looks like the kobolds have taken a lot of books. There are whole bookshelves emptied out. You should probably see what Brother Paxton wants you to do about it.$B$BWhile you\'re here, can I talk to you about tradeskills? I\'d be happy to answer any questions you have, or point you toward the local trainers.', 0),
(92432, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(92459, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(92706, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Finally, somebody killed that thing! Do you know how hard it is to get a crew in the water when everyone in town\'s crying "Shark!"all the time?$B$BI might just put that monster\'s fin into a soup for dinner tonight, just to have the last laugh.', 0),
(92744, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I see... these gills appear to be healthy, for now. But we must not be complacent.', 0),
(92909, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thanks a bunch! I\'ll get to work on an escape plan. In the meantime, take this!', 0),
(93176, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(93224, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(93225, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(94872, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(95212, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These pelts will make excellent saddles. You\'ve done the Alliance proud, $C!', 0),
(95213, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The $R turns pale as he sees the empty keg.>$B$B...Where did you find this?', 0),
(95214, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'That should be all the stolen powder. Thank you, $C.$B$BPlease accept this reward, and... I\'d appreciate if you didn\'t mention this little incident to anyone.', 0),
(95328, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What an interesting specimen. From underneath the Whispering Forest, you say? It\'s no secret that foul place is touched by the void.$B$BI welcome the opportunity to explore the mysteries of shadow, $C. Allow me to offer you payment for what you\'ve found.', 0),
(95494, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, these look like they will do nicely. I have an arrangement with a local tanner to deliver these raw hides in exchange for various finished leather goods that I use as part of my trade.$B$BI\'ve never come up short on my end of the arrangement, and even with my injury I do not intend to start now.', 0),
(95495, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Vrang sent you then? Very well. I appreciate you delivering these hides to me. It\'s unfortunate that Vrang couldn\'t make the journey himself. There is a matter I wish to speak with him about.', 0),
(95508, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well, looks like we are all alive. I... knew that someday that would catch up to me. I\'m in your debt for your help here today.$B$BPlease, take this. It\'s not much, but its the least I can do.$B$BSafe travels, $C.', 0),
(95621, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So they are looking for a deserter... Well, it seems that the past has finally caught up to me.', 0),
(95774, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I will place these adornments with my wife\'s memorial, so that I never forget her. My blood will always run hot with revenge!$B$BYou have done me... done us... a great favor, Johnathon.', 0),
(95981, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ever since the barrier went down around Dalaran, the Kirin Tor have maintained a death grip on the roads. They\'re paranoid about something, that much is certain.$B$BFor now, however, the why is irrelevant.', 0),
(96137, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(96138, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(96391, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Juding by this map, it certainly looks like these Dark Irons are planning some sort of incursion into the vaults beneath Ironforge. The band ye busted up to the east must be a scouting force.$B$BThank ye for bringing me this. If we hurry, we might be able to beat them to whatever their goal is down there.', 0),
(96408, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Greetings, friend. How are ya?', 0),
(96821, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The peons have been scared to travel south for some time, Joruus. Now that you\'ve cleared the path a bit, we can get them back to work.', 0),
(96876, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'My pack! When I dropped it to run from that huge spider, I thought I\'d never see it again. You really are a hero!', 0),
(96877, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What a trophy, $C! That must have been some fight!', 0),
(96895, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Stay low and try not to be seen, $C. These cultists are not to be trifled with.', 0),
(96896, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I plan to stay here for a time and speak with more of my friends, but I will return to Light\'s Hope Chapel in Eastern Plaguelands soon enough. Should you ever find yourself out that way, please do say hello. We could use always use more help from able-bodied adventurers.', 0),
(96897, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for your aid, $C. If we do not wish to see Lordaeron\'s history repeat itself, we\'ve got to be vigilant when threats like this spring up.', 0),
(96898, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you. This should slow the efforts of the scourge in this area. I suspect the denizens of Tirisfal will be pulling these crystals out of the ground for years, but removing the most conspicuous of them can only help.', 0),
(96899, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This place is full of memories for me. This place was once held by the Argent Dawn. It was here from here that we prepared for many battles and skirmishes against the scourge during their most recent push into Tirisfal Glades.$B$BWhen we withdrew to the Plaguelands I feared it would fall into disrepair. My fear was well-founded, but I am glad that Danitha and her paladins have taken over stewardship of it now.$B$BShe even named the keep after... a mutual friend.', 0),
(97003, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Impressive, $C. None will doubt my tales when I return to Orgrimmar with this grim proof of the existence of these abominations. Rest assured this glory is yours however, and I will speak loudly of your deeds.$B$BLok-tar!', 0),
(97005, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'My dead men will rest easier knowing that there is one less of these monsters in the world. You\'ve done well, and are a true and stalwart defender of the alliance. Thank you.$B$BGo with honor, Gryma.', 0),
(97223, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you, $N. I am happy we will be able to preserve her bloodline and raise them to be our allies. You have done a great service for our tribe.', 0),
(97236, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'My, my. How I do love surprises, $N.$B$BThis specimen will surely help further my studies.', 0),
(97246, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Of course. Migi\'s parents and I have an arrangement to give Migi a bagged lunch every day, but I can only ensure the boy gets his food if he actually comes in to pick it up.$B$BSometimes, he doesn\'t pick up his meal multiple times a week, and I wonder where he gets the energy to stay out and play.', 0),
(97249, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Borstan\'s Meats? Is that for one of us?$B$BOh!$B$BWow... this smells really good! Yummy.$B$BThanks for bringing me my lunch. I can tell what Borstan is going to be serving daily when my friends and I walk the road to Grommash Hold, by the smells alone. This tastes like my favorite, the sweetglaze! But it\'s different. I like the strong flavored crumbs.$B$BIf it\'s going to be this tasty every day, I think we need to stop our game to take our lunch together!', 0),
(97250, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So the rumors were true! I expected as much, tensions have been rising along the eastern coast for some time. I knew it would only be a matter of time before conflict crept into our territory.$B$BHowever, I am skeptical that we played a role in the tavern\'s destruction. Too many Horde civilians rely on that route for trade and travel. Perhaps you could investigate further if you find the time.$B$BIn any case, today\'s deed is a victory for the Horde, and a stern warning to the Alliance!', 0),
(97275, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Grorru--whaa?$B$BYou say Yelmak made this potion from speargrass and cattail with no other reagents? I didn\'t know chemists had any real need for these common plants we see every day.$B$BMaybe he\'s right. There could be a lot I\'m missing out on by skipping to the most rare and least-studied flora first.$B$BDrakath, take your pick from one of these potions I brewed earlier. I appreciate you taking the time to visit our shop.', 0),
(97281, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Woah, where did you find a neat thing like that? Ya know it reminds me of the other thing my boss Gazlowe always used to tell me...', 0),
(97282, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hey, thanks pal! You\'ve been a really big help to me here and I appreciate it.$B$BHere\'s to hoping I can get this all charged up using these organs. I bet it\'ll make those no good harpies think twice about attacking my caravan again. I sure hope this works.$B$BEither way you\'ve done your side of the deal. Take this for your trouble.', 0),
(97287, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(97290, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Not cooperating, eh? Excellent. I always love a challenge.', 0),
(97558, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, excellent! Thank you for acquiring these. I can promise they will be put to good use.', 0),
(97891, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, marvelous! I had been waiting for Alessandro\'s potion to arrive. The last six he sent destabilized along the way, but you\'ve made it just in time!$B$BHere, take this for your effort. That is all for now, unless you have other business with me?$B$BIf not, remove yourself so I may continue my experiments unhindered.', 0),
(97894, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Old Borgy sent you? Always looking out for me.$B$BWe could certainly use another set of hands around here. Business has all but stopped with the recent tragedy, and I think you could help set things right.', 0),
(97914, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Baros opens the letter and begins to read it, his smile fading.>', 0),
(97926, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Sad news indeed. Still, I thank you for making the journey.$B$BWith neither Stormwind nor Darnassus coming to aid us, it seems that Auberdine\'s fate is our own to decide.', 0),
(97985, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98013, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Do not fret, young one. To pillage one\'s own home for some dark master...$B$BIt is unforgivable.', 0),
(98025, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It is good to know that issue has been taken care of, but it saddens me that we could not find another way. Jai\'vhanel had been somewhat of a guardian of this area for quite some time, and I am not sure what could have caused her decent into madness.$B$BRegardless, thank you for your service today, $C. The roads to Auberdine are safe for travel once again.', 0),
(98028, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Onu appears surprised--or as surprised as an ancient can appear.>$B$BStairs descending down in Mathystra? Could be it be?$B$B<Onu shakes his head.>$B$BI must confer with the others on this. For now, know that it is good you uncovered this before the naga... or their cult allies.$B$BPlease accept this as thanks for your efforts. It is no small feat to defeat an elemental guardian.', 0),
(98042, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Thundris does not speak for some time.>$B$BThis bears the mark of an ancient evil, $C. I will see it brought to Darnassus at once for further study.$B$BAnde\'thoras-ethil.', 0),
(98046, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Do not mind the Arch Druid, Sneaky. He bears the weight of much in Malfurion\'s absence.$B$BWait! Some drops yet remain in the phial! Perhaps that is why his incantation failed?', 0),
(98059, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98065, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Staghelm has done much in my beloved\'s absence, but he is not Malfurion. And he does not run the affairs of Darnassus--that burden is mine alone.$B$B<Tyrande\'s face settles.>$B$BI apologize. As you have likely seen, we have many challenges to overcome.$B$BFandral is Arch Druid for now, and I ask you respect his station. But his doings pertain to druidism, and mine not only to Elune but indeed to lead our people as she wills.$B$BEvery drop of this water is blessed by our goddess. I thank you for saving it.', 0),
(98070, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98072, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98094, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98095, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98155, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98189, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98209, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98216, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98219, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98230, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98240, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98245, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98251, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98252, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98282, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98283, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98291, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98297, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98298, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It appears I get the last laugh after all, haha! Arugal truly was a fool. And I, Dalar Dawnweaver, have exposed him as the fraud he is.$B$BThese pieces are all the proof I need that the curse has nothing to do with that blithering dolt.$B$BRegrettably, that means his remedy is also worth nothing. It seems the search for a solution to the worgen curse continues.', 0),
(98299, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It seems the Gilneans are not too keen on allowing anyone past their wall. That is fortunate, I suppose. It means there is likely no chance for the worgen curse to spread to their city.$B$BCan you imagine the depravity if an entire kingdom were infected?', 0),
(98300, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98310, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98313, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98322, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ol\' Whitebeard sent ya, aye?$B$BI got his report, alright. This whole situation\'s a mess!', 0),
(98326, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yer a real lifesaver, Leif!$B$BMy husband would just laugh it off, but I couldn\'t bare tellin\' him he has to spend another night on the lake. Maybe now we can enjoy a real feast.', 0),
(98391, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I am glad you arrived so quickly. The Sisterhood requires your aid.', 0),
(98392, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Arynia investigates the amulets.>$B$BDo you see the foul green swirls within the gems? This is indeed fel moss corruption at work.$B$BI have heard similar reports from Shadowglen and elsewhere in the boughs of this substance turning our very world against us.$B$BI will inform my superiors of this at once.', 0),
(98403, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I should have known this was being used to twist the spiders of this land.$B$BI have heard whispers of this substance being the source of much of the corruption plaguing us. Though this is not the original, it is an older sample and may yield more information than what we have obtained so far.$B$BNormally I would have you send this to Darnassus for further study. However, it is best we kept this quiet for the moment, or Dolanaar will never recover its reputation.$B$BI trust you to do the same.', 0),
(98407, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Quite the armful you have.$B$BWhile this doesn\'t solve our problem out here, I can rest comfortably knowing we\'ve discouraged them pushing any further. Great work, $N.', 0),
(98418, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98435, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, no wonder there is such joy running through the streams of Mulgore. You have done a great service today. The wells provide much for not only our people, but to the wildlife we depend on for food, clothing, and companionship.$B$BIt is my humble pleasure to honor Mull\'s request. Please, accept this token of my gratitude.', 0),
(98459, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Bart unwraps the gift.>$B$BWhy that no good, son of a--$B$BDid he even tell you that HE is the one who cheats at poker?! I only won enough money to buy the Maiden\'s Virtue after we kicked him out of our poker circle!$B$BI swear, the next time I see that absolute waste of seawater--$B$BI\'m sorry, I\'m sorry. I shouldn\'t shoot the messenger. On behalf of the crew of the Maiden\'s Virtue--finest ship in the Great Sea--welcome to Menethil Harbor!', 0),
(98461, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Tarrel reads the note.>$B$BOh... oh my. Poor Hollee.$B$BShe always did have a bit of a thing for me. And, truth be told, there was a time where I would have reciprocated. But I\'m married. Happily married!$B$BI think the best thing to do here is not to reply. I don\'t know how to let her down, and I have far more pressing things to worry about here! My wife is missing!', 0),
(98463, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hand in the quest.', 0),
(98545, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thanks for delivering this, pal.$B$BWait... he said I\'d tip you? I didn\'t agree to that!$B$BFine. Take your pick of this junk in the lost and found. You\'d be surprised how many of these Forsaken leave their stuff laying around after getting haircuts. There\'s a joke here about them being brainless, but I suspect in a lot of cases it might actually be true.', 0),
(99046, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Elune\'s grace... I shall not die... alone...', 0),
(99047, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The harpies have become afflicted by the same foulness showing up throughout the forest. I\'m sure that is what ails Sentinel Eralya as well.$B$BWe must hurry. It won\'t be long before she succumbs to her injuries.', 0),
(99048, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Heglan\'s body lies cold within the wreckage of the hut.$B$BWhatever killed her doesn\'t seem to be human. There may be signs of what happened nearby.', 0),
(99050, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for your help. Please, accept this to help with the costs of the vial and water.$B$BNow, to make the salve. It should only take a moment.', 0),
(99073, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Eralya\'s breath calms quickly as you help her ingest the salve. She may not survive, but is at relative peace.>', 0),
(99141, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I should have known better than to think an abomination could write anything of use. Let us keep that lapse of judgment between us.$B$BYou have pleased me, and therefore pleased the Dark Lady. Perhaps there is hope for you.', 0),
(99152, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done, recruit. We might just make something out of you yet.$B$BWith these bones we may be able to better understand how such a threat was able to go unnoticed for so long.', 0),
(99156, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You are a testament to the cunning and coordination that all Forsaken possess--something the mindless Scourge will never have.$B$BPlease accept this as thanks for your efforts, as promised.', 0),
(99158, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah. Candles from Ironforge.$B$BWhile I am mostly able to live independently in my hermitage, there are a few key things that I appreciate from the city and the pious.', 0);
